<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.980
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.320
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.320
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.310
What was that?!

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.590
I don't know! Let's just get out of...

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.240
Hey...

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:30.500
Don't forgive the humans!

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:36.440
CHAPTER 45

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:41.510
THE TRUTH LIES IN
THE THICKET OF THE MANNEN-DAKE

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:51.500
We've come pretty deep into the mountains.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:55.270
"The <i>yokai</i>, Mannen-Dake is attacking us.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.610
Come to the bamboo thicket."

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.550
TO GEGEGE NO KITARO

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:01.280
Dad, what's the Mannen-Dake like?

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.700
It's a bamboo <i>yokai</i>
that's over 10,000 years old.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.920
I hear it's a terrifying <i>yokai</i>
that drains the life force

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.390
of humans who get lost in the thicket.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.960
That's...

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.490
Hey, Kitaro!

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.720
I see you read the letter.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.450
Thanks!

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.440
So, this is...

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:35.190
Kubota-san from the tourism board,

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:38.480
and the Kanais,
who own this bamboo thicket.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.160
What's going on?

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.660
They want to make this bamboo thicket
a tourist spot.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.370
So, in the process,

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:51.710
they asked me to check
if the Mannen-Dake really is here.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:57.510
Apparently, many people who enter
this bamboo thicket have gone missing.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.960
Just the other day,
two of our surveyors...

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:03.180
Were they attacked by the Mannen-Dake?

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:06.970
Oh please, Kubota-san.
It doesn't even exist.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.220
It exists.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:11.730
The Mannen-Dake exists.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:16.690
Now, now, everyone.
There's no point arguing here.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.360
That's right. Let's get this over with.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:23.110
Kitaro-chan, hurry up!

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:26.510
Why do I have to work with him?

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:33.290
It seems like something is
definitely hiding here.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.960
Yes, Dad.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.480
Where are we going?

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.800
The home of the previous owner
of this bamboo thicket, Daikichi Kanai.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.970
Currently, it belongs to his son.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.680
Daikichi used to own this entire area.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.040
But he disappeared ten years ago.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.460
Wh-What's that?

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:05.280
<i>Get out...</i>

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.700
<i>Humans, get out...</i>

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.750
I-I just heard something.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:14.020
Th-That's just your imagination.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:17.210
See? Just like I told you.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.590
The Mannen-Dake really exists!

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.720
That's enough out of you!

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:27.140
Kiyomi, it's not too late.
Let's go back! Let's cancel development!

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:31.020
Don't be stupid! Such a thing can't exist!

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:32.060
We're going!

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.580
Kiyomi, wait!

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.120
Kitaro, what's up?

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.290
Nothing. Let's keep going.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:43.380
Did you find something?

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.830
We're going to die.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:53.680
HUMANS, GET OUT

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.790
The Mannen-Dake's going to kill us all!

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.160
I-It must be someone's prank!

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.480
B-B-But, Ma'am...!

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.990
This is...

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:31.780
Woah, what is this?

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.330
How could this happen?

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:40.250
I see. Dad really was
killed by the Mannen-Dake...

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:42.880
Masahiko-san, what do you mean?

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:47.800
This place... This room was
my dad's study.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.880
Daikichi-san's room?

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:53.850
Dad really loved this bamboo thicket.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.910
He lived here for a long time.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:02.020
But ten years ago,
he suddenly disappeared.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:07.950
There had always been rumors that
the Mannen-Dake lived in this thicket.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:12.030
I had misgivings about
leaving him here alone.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:16.810
But he was so stubborn,
he refused to leave this house.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:21.100
He should have left this place sooner.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:24.960
If only I'd been more insistent then.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.800
This wouldn't have happened.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.570
Masahiko-san.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:34.220
He was a little strange,
but he was a dad I admired.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:41.690
He'd donate the fortune he'd made over
a generation to poor kids and the elderly.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.590
That's the kind dad he was.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.570
Dad...

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.090
Oh, here you are.

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:51.450
Wh-What is this room?!

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.950
The Mannen-Dake is sending us a warning.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.950
"This will happen to you, too!"

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.420
K-Kiyomi-san, let's just go!

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.460
N-No! We just got here!

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.570
There's no way the Mannen-Dake exists.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:18.950
Masahiko-san?

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:24.230
Honey, what are you doing?

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.750
Honey...?

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.700
He's turned to bamboo!

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.540
Hold on a minute.

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:41.700
This wasn't done by the Mannen-Dake.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:44.880
Kitaro, what are you talking about?

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.500
A man was turned into bamboo!

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.550
I thought something was strange
from the start.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:55.760
Despite such blatant warnings from
the Mannen-Dake,

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.990
from inside this house...

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.270
I couldn't sense any <i>yokai</i> activity.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.750
Wait. That means...

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:06.230
Yeah.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:10.020
This was done by a human
pretending to be a <i>yokai</i>.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:14.860
There!

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:21.890
Honey?

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:26.710
Do you know what you've done?!

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:30.040
You tried to trick us!

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.760
<i>Humans, get out...</i>

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.350
Now that you listen to it, it's his voice.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:38.550
What an elaborate setup.

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:40.520
I had to...

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:45.770
I had to get all of you to give up
developing this bamboo thicket.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.560
Why go so far?

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:51.820
I wanted to protect
Dad's bamboo thicket no matter what.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.150
Are you still going on about that?!

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.570
Your dad is missing!

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.570
But he might come back!

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:02.410
I sold all the other land like you said!

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:06.330
But this place...
I can't do that to this place!

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:09.710
This is the bamboo thicket that Dad loved!

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:13.530
This is ridiculous.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:18.910
Kubota-san, when we get back,
let's discuss the contract.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:22.930
Now we know there's no Mannen-Dake here.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:26.140
W-Wait, Kiyomi.
The Mannen-Dake really does exist!

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:30.860
What? You're still trying to trick us
after all that?

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:32.230
Kiyomi-san.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:37.220
When we entered this bamboo thicket,
I'm sure I sensed <i>yokai</i> activity.

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:40.860
There is definitely a <i>yokai</i> here.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:44.970
What?! Now don't you start.

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:49.790
This is...!

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:57.550
Don't forgive the humans.

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:02.120
Don't forgive the humans!

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.560
<i>YOKAI</i> MANNEN-DAKE

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:11.060
FIGHTING WITH <i>YOKAI</i> MANNEN-DAKE!

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:09.960
<i>"I sense </i>yokai<i> activity."</i>

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:10.960
<i>"I didn't see that..."</i>

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:15.940
What are these things?

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.260
Don't forgive the humans!

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:21.530
Oh, what?

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:25.450
You had a big gimmick like this
saved for last?

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.290
Keep away from those things!

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:29.160
What?!

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:30.230
Kiyomi!

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:37.320
Kiyomi!

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:40.170
Wait! This isn't what you promised!

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:42.820
Help!

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.250
Kubota-san!

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.310
Hey, they're increasing in number!

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:55.320
Dad, these are...

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:59.860
They must be the people
who got lost in this bamboo thicket.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:04.740
Hey, what do we do? At this rate
we'll be turned to bamboo, too!

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.830
Sorry, I'm busy here.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:09.200
If you've got business, maybe later...

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:24.180
Kitaro, we'll have to find
where the Mannen-Dake itself is.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:26.070
Head to the back garden!

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:30.560
Up the small path from the back garden
is where the Mannen-Dake lives.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.210
Masahiko-san?

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.820
Talk later! Let's go, Kitaro!

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:38.000
Right!

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:53.160
Masahiko-san, why do you know about
the Mannen-Dake?

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:58.790
After my dad disappeared,
I came here a few times.

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:03.670
Knowing my dad,
I thought he'd wander back eventually.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:08.330
Then I was attacked
by those bamboo people.

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.810
Don't forgive the humans!

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.440
H-H-Help me!

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:19.230
I-I just came here looking for my dad!

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:21.320
Your dad?

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:22.610
That's right.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.820
He lived in the house
in this bamboo thicket.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:29.470
Are you Daikichi's son?

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:32.450
You know my dad?

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:35.580
I see. You're Daikichi's son.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.900
Thank you for coming.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:41.590
That's when I found out.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:45.090
My dad loved this bamboo thicket,

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:51.350
and the master of the thicket,
the Mannen-Dake, considered him a friend.

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:55.850
You're saying Daikichi-san was friends
with the Mannen-Dake?!

00:13:55.850 --> 00:14:00.110
I've been meeting
the Mannen-Dake regularly since then.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.070
I'm sorry for not telling you.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:07.610
Does the Mannen-Dake know
all that you've been doing here?

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.200
It was my idea.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:14.370
I said I'd get them to
call off development.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:18.540
In return
it wouldn't harm Kiyomi and the others.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.880
But, because I failed,

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.550
the bamboo people came out.

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:27.130
And Kiyomi was turned into one...

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.390
I'm sorry, Kiyomi...

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.780
Kiyomi...

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:40.790
So this is the Mannen-Dake.

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:43.400
MANNEN-DAKE

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.250
Masahiko.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:47.200
Who are you?

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.030
I'm GeGeGe no Kitaro.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.780
Mannen-Dake, stop this!

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.390
I refuse!

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.220
Kitaro-san!

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:57.390
Hair Needles!

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.920
That hardly tickles!

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:04.550
I'll impale you!

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:07.650
Remote Controlled Geta!

00:15:09.910 --> 00:15:12.010
It's no good! There's no effect!

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:17.640
Kitaro!

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:19.480
Kitaro-san!

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.530
You'll become bamboo, too!

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:36.910
Mannen-Dake, that's enough!

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:41.350
I'll make you part of my body. Be honored!

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:43.420
Kitaro!

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:58.430
The Mannen-Dake's in pain?

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:04.810
That's it! He's absorbing <i>yokai</i> power from
the Mannen-Dake where they're connected!

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:40.980
Mannen-Dake, you were able to
befriend Daikichi-san.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.860
Why do you hate humans so much?

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:46.230
You can't understand my...

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:49.820
My... My and Masahiko's ...

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:53.030
The pain in our hearts.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:55.010
The pain in your hearts?

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:59.180
Daikichi did not go missing.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:03.460
Daikichi was murdered by a human.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:04.790
Murdered?!

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:09.360
Daikichi was my only friend.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:13.300
Hello, Bamboo-san. How are you?

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:19.050
Daikichi loved this bamboo thicket
and understood me.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:23.710
Don't you get lonely
living in that house alone?

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.830
I don't need any sympathy.

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:30.570
I've got you, Bamboo-san.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:36.200
Daikichi was someone irreplaceable to me.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:38.200
But, one day...

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.310
I'm heading out for a bit.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:44.040
Daikichi never returned.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.210
Instead...

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:49.210
That night, a strange man appeared.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:55.590
The man with the large mark on his
left arm buried something in the thicket.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:59.090
Later on I learned that

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:02.410
it was Daikichi's corpse.

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:06.850
I hated humans from
the bottom of my heart.

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:10.940
So that's why
you started attacking humans.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:16.570
Masahiko-san, why did you keep
Daikichi-san's murder a secret?

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.910
I heard it from a <i>yokai</i>.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:22.370
Even if I told the police,
they'd never believe me.

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:23.990
Besides...

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:29.630
if word of my dad's murder got out,
lots of people would come to investigate.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:33.010
This bamboo thicket might get damaged.

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:34.840
That can't happen!

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.340
Masahiko-san...

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:41.100
I just want my dad to rest in peace
in this bamboo thicket.

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:44.060
In this bamboo thicket that my dad loved.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:48.520
Mannen-Dake, please don't hate humans.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:49.560
Masahiko...

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:54.070
I'll protect this bamboo thicket
in my dad's place!

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:09.420
Kiyomi!

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:10.330
Honey!

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:11.920
I was so scared!

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.230
Are you all right?

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:17.890
I'm sorry. I didn't believe you.

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:20.860
Let's not develop this place after all.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:24.930
He wishes to quietly protect
Daikichi-san's body.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:30.350
I'm sure the Mannen-Dake understands
Masahiko-san's wishes.

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:35.610
Yes. I'm sure the Mannen-Dake won't
attack humans unprovoked anymore.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:43.760
I guess we never found out who
Daikichi-san's killer was.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.430
Kitaro, what's wrong?

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:56.150
Honey, hurry!

00:19:58.490 --> 00:19:59.680
Masahiko-san.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:00.630
Yes?

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:03.470
May I see your left arm?

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:05.890
What's this all of a sudden?

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:09.390
You never wanted to protect
Daikichi-san's bamboo thicket.

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:15.920
Letting word of Daikichi-san's murder
get out was inconvenient for you.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:22.150
Masahiko-san, it's not too late.
Go to the police and pay for your crime.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:26.680
Humans must face judgement
under human laws.

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:29.540
What's so funny?

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:34.670
Of course I never cared anything about
this old bamboo thicket.

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:36.170
What?

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:40.920
My dad...
Sure the old man was a great man and all.

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:44.640
He protected the bamboo thicket
and the children.

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:48.140
He spread his love around to
all the poor people.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:53.640
On top of that, he was a fool who said
he'd donate his fortune after he died.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:55.400
That's crazy!

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.940
I'm his son!

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:59.650
It should all be mine!

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:04.660
It was a shock when
the Mannen-Dake attacked me.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.410
But it turned out to be the perfect cover.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:11.120
With the Mannen-Dake here,
no one will enter.

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:15.210
The obtrusive old man dies
and his fortune is all mine.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:16.630
And...

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:19.460
the truth is literally
buried in the thicket!

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.990
That's it. I've heard enough.

